# Milestone: v0.10.11-channel-and-isA
# Covers: Lobby is an alias for the global Realm; bindings in Lobby are visible
#         globally and vice versa.
#
# blocked: Lobby readonly (defer-v1.x per D5 verdict)
# matrix-row: stdlib-lobby
#
# Reason: D5 (v0.10.11 W5) unfroze Object only; Lobby remains in the readonly
# cohort.  The `Lobby.lobbies` session-registry invariant is load-bearing for
# the REPL session-management contract: Lobby.lobbies is written by the C REPL
# layer at session open/close, and allowing arbitrary script-side slot
# installation on Lobby could corrupt the registry.  Sandboxing policy for
# post-D5 Lobby is deferred to v1.x (if a concrete threat model warrants it,
# a capability-gated unfreeze can be introduced).  Until then, `Lobby.x = v`
# raises TypeError.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate when Lobby readonly is revisited at v1.x):
#   Lobby.x = 123;
#   x
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] 123
